{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ring homomorphism ring homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Ring Homomorphism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ring Homomorphism","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","First Isomorphism Theorem for Rings","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ring homomorphism ring homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Ring Homomorphism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ring Homomorphism","heading":"Ring Homomorphism","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A ring homomorphism is a map between rings that preserves addition, multiplication, and the [[Ring Identity]]. Its kernel is an [[Ideal]] of the source ring, and its image is a subring of the target.\n\nThe kernel records which elements become zero. The [[First Isomorphism Theorem for Rings]] identifies the image with the source modulo that kernel, connecting homomorphisms directly to [[Quotient Ring]]s.\n\nThe book develops ring homomorphisms in parallel with group homomorphisms: kernels are ideals, images are subrings, and the source modulo its kernel is isomorphic to the image. This parallel motivates both quotient rings and the ring version of the fundamental homomorphism theorem.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","First Isomorphism Theorem for Rings","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ring homomorphism ring homomorphism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ring Homomorphism.md","fileName":"Ring Homomorphism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ring Homomorphism","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","First Isomorphism Theorem for Rings","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}